menu "KAI watch"

    config KAI_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Leave this empty and the radio never comes up: the watch runs off
            its own boot clock and the WiFi corner readout stays dim, which is
            what that dimming is for. Fill it in and the watch joins the
            network and asks SNTP what time it is.

    config KAI_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default ""

    config KAI_SNTP_SERVER
        string "SNTP server"
        default "pool.ntp.org"

    config KAI_TIMEZONE
        string "POSIX TZ string"
        default "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3"
        help
            SNTP hands out UTC and the device has no locale to convert it
            with, so the zone is compiled in. The default is central Europe
            with EU daylight saving.

endmenu
